INTRODUCE INTRO INTRODUCTIONS

Usage: introduce <person>
       introduce list
       introduce forget <name>

Until someone introduces themselves to you, you see their short description
instead of their name. Introducing yourself teaches the recipient your name;
you still need their introduction to learn theirs. NPCs and immortals are exempt.
Target strangers using words from their visible description, such as human.
Introductions are remembered when you reconnect. You cannot introduce yourself
while wearing a disguise.

See also: DISGUISE
#0
DISGUISE DISGUISES

Usage: disguise <race> | <age> | <gender> | <feature:adjective> | <feature:adjective>
       disguise <race>
       disguise descriptors [feature]
       disguise remove

Example: disguise human | adolescent | female | hair:43 | eyes:2

Type disguise alone to see eligible races. You may appear as a humanoid of your
own size. Ages: adult, adolescent, middle-aged, old-aged, venerable.
Genders: neutral, male, female. Select up to two feature:adjective pairs using
the same choices as your normal short description. Use disguise descriptors to
list feature types, and disguise descriptors hair to list hair adjectives.
For example, hair:43 selects short silver hair; eyes:2 selects green eyes.
Numeric feature IDs also work (6:43 means hair:43). Use none to omit a feature.
A race alone uses your actual age, gender, and natural descriptor selections.

Applying a disguise uses your Disguise ability once. Each person who first sees
that disguise gets one opposing Perception check; ties see through it. Looking
again or reconnecting does not grant another check. Remove and reapply a disguise
to create a new instance. Applying and removing each use a standard action.

A fooled observer sees your disguised description, even if they know your name.
Someone who sees through it sees your known name or real short description,
followed by a separate line describing the disguise. This never teaches a name.
True sight automatically sees through disguises without a perception roll.

Disguises change appearance only, granting no racial traits or attribute changes.
Remove a disguise before using wildshape or shapechange or introducing yourself.

See also: INTRODUCE
#0
DISGUISESELF DISGUISE_SELF

Usage: cast 'disguise self'
       disguise dismiss disguise self

For ten minutes per caster level you receive +10 to your Disguise skill.
This spell does not change your visible appearance or active race by itself.
Apply a disguise normally to use the skill bonus in its application roll.

See also: DISGUISE, ALTERSELF
#0
ALTERSELF ALTER_SELF

Usage: cast 'alter self' <player-selectable race>
       disguise dismiss alter self

Your active race changes to the selected race for one minute per caster level.
You may choose any player-selectable race, including locked races. A Small form
grants +2 Dexterity; a Medium or larger form grants +2 Strength. Both use the
racial bonus type. Tiny or smaller forms grant neither attribute bonus.

Ordinary observers see the changed race, which Perception cannot see through.
True sight shows your original form and separately describes your altered form. Other disguise details, such as descriptors,
age, and gender, can still be seen through under the normal disguise rules.
The spell does not reset an existing disguise's perception checks.

Disguise Self and Alter Self can coexist. Expiration, dispelling, or dismissal
restores your original active race and removes the attribute bonus.

See also: DISGUISESELF, DISGUISE
#0
TRUEFORM TRUEFORMS TRUESIGHT

True sight shows a person's original form, including through disguises, Alter
Self, wildshape, polymorph, and other shapechanges. It also shows a separate line
describing the current altered form, so you know how the person appears to others.
Any mundane disguise is described separately as well.

Knowing the true form does not teach an unknown person's name. The introduction
rules still apply. True sight changes what you perceive, leaving the person's
actual transformed race, size, and abilities unchanged.

See also: INTRODUCE, DISGUISE, ALTERSELF
#0
IRDA IRDAFORM
Irda are an advanced race with +2 Dexterity, Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma.
They can change humanoid form at will, including apparent age, gender and
features from the normal character descriptor menus.

  disguise form <race> | <age> | <gender> | <feature:adjective> | <feature:adjective>
  disguise form human | old-aged | female | hair:43 | eyes:2
  disguise form remove

Use disguise descriptors [feature] to see available descriptor choices.
Any humanoid race is allowed. A race alone uses your natural age, gender and
features. Use none to omit a feature. Each change takes a standard action.

No Disguise training or opposed Disguise/Perception check is required. Your
form persists until you change or remove it, including across reconnects.
True Sight reveals your natural form alongside your assumed appearance.
Return to natural form before advancing or using another transformation.

See also: DISGUISE, TRUEFORM, INTRODUCE
#0
SIVAK SIVAKDRACONIAN SIVAKFORMS

Sivak draconians are Large advanced characters with +2 Strength, Dexterity,
Constitution and Intelligence. They cost 8,000 account XP to unlock and gain
+3 natural armor, flight, ultravision, disease immunity,
draconian spell resistance, bite, draconic devotion, gallop and Improved Trip.

  disguise forms                List learned humanoid appearances.
  disguise form <number>        Assume a learned appearance.
  disguise form remove          Return to natural Sivak form.

Personally killing a humanoid NPC or PC teaches you its appearance. Non-humanoids,
self-kills and arena defeats do not grant forms. You do not gain forms from
another group member's or a pet's kills. All genders can use this ability.

Forms reproduce the victim's appearance, visible gender and size, without copying
their equipment, name, skills or spells. You cannot freely edit a learned form.
Changing form takes a standard action, without a Disguise or Perception roll.
True Sight shows your natural form and your assumed appearance together.

Your learned forms AND currently assumed form are saved to your player file.
They persist across sessions and server restarts. Returning to natural form
does not erase the collection; you can reuse any learned form later.

Return to natural form before advancing or using another transformation.

See also: DISGUISE, IRDA, TRUEFORM, FLY, BITE, TRIP
#0
AURAK AURAKDRACONIAN RACE-AURAK-DRACONIAN

Auraks are the strongest advanced draconian race: Medium, wingless masters of
magic with +2 Dexterity, +4 Intelligence and +4 Charisma. Unlocking costs 15,000
account experience; their level adjustment is 4.

They gain +6 natural armor, spell resistance of 12 + character level, ultravision,
disease immunity, bite, draconic devotion, Combat Casting and Improved Initiative.
They cannot fly naturally.

Use cast to invoke racial spells, without a caster class or prepared slots:
  Level 1: aurak energy ray, aurak breath, disguise self, magic missile
  Level 3: charm, mirror image
  Level 5: fireball, dispel magic
  Level 7: greater invisibility
  Level 9: dominate person (once per rolling 24 real hours)

Examples:
  cast 'aurak energy ray' <enemy>
  cast 'aurak breath'
  cast 'greater invisibility'
  cast 'dominate person' <enemy>

Energy ray uses a swift action for one ranged touch attack dealing 4d6 force
damage. Breath affects
eligible enemies in the room: Fortitude negates a temporary 1d2 Strength penalty
and blindness lasting 1d4 rounds. Poison immunity protects against the breath;
blindness immunity protects against its blinding effect. Breath recharges after
1d4 combat rounds. Neither attack costs Aurak spell points. Other at-will racial
spells share 10 points, costing their base wizard circle per cast. The full pool
refills five minutes after its first use. Use innates to check remaining points.
Disguise self, magic missile and charm cost 1; mirror image costs 2; fireball and
dispel magic cost 3; greater invisibility costs 4. Normal casting actions apply.

Racial magic uses your character level and Charisma. Spell points, breath and domination
recharge times are saved in your player file and persist across sessions.
Disguise Self grants +10 Disguise, using the normal disguise command for looks.

On death, Auraks release 3d6 force damage against eligible enemies in the room,
with Reflex saves for half damage. Normal equipment and resurrection rules apply.

See also: DISGUISE, DISGUISESELF, CAST, BITE
